# UNAUTHENTICATED surface. The org_id ARGUMENT is still accepted (no compile break), it
# is simply never applied. This is the T74-T77 "drop-the-filter-must-flip-a-named-test"
# org-scope pin, generalized to a derived read action instead of a resource policy.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/scopes/cms_kb_scope_test.exs test/samen/web/portal_kb_live_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: org A's portal read shows ONLY org A's public article, never org B's
# MUST_FAIL: org B's portal read shows its OWN article, not org A's (both sides proven live)
# MUST_FAIL: org A's portal never shows org B's public article, browse OR deflect
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/cms/blueprint.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/cms/blueprint.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/cms/blueprint.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/cms/blueprint.ex
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@ defmodule Samen.Scopes.Cms.PublicPostFilter do

     Ash.Query.filter(
       query,
-      org_id == ^org_id and status == :published and visibility == :public
+      status == :published and visibility == :public
     )
   end
 end
